cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived KIN-SYS Protocol release."
title: "KIN-SYS Protocol: Provider-Neutral Governed Execution Prototype"
authors:
  - family-names: Kagoro
    given-names: Joel
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe933212-pixel/KIN-SYS-PROTOCOL"
abstract: >-
  KIN-SYS is a provider-neutral protocol architecture for governing and
  verifying digital instructions across institutional and jurisdictional
  boundaries. This release provides a runnable local synthetic reference
  prototype with MINAH-first instruction ingress, identity and action-specific
  authority gates, CEE-controlled execution with IVM transition checks,
  durable local SQLite journals, explicit decision outcomes, operation
  inspection, and bounded recovery tooling. It is a research/reference
  prototype, not a production deployment. External identity, authority, legal,
  institutional, and payment integrations are synthetic or test doubles.
keywords:
  - governed execution
  - institutional coordination
  - verifiable execution
  - distributed systems
  - digital sovereignty
  - protocol architecture
  - East Africa
